{"name":"Windjammer","hex":"#62a5df","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"windjammer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who plays a wind instrument, especially a bugler in the army.","A sailing ship; especially a large, iron-hulled, square-rigged ship with three or more masts."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/windjammer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Windjammer","blocks":[{"text":"A windjammer is a commercial sailing ship with multiple masts, however rigged. The informal term \"windjammer\" arose during the transition from the Age of Sail to the Age of Steam during the 19th century. The Oxford English Dictionary records the term \"wind jammer\" with reference to a ship from 1878 and nautical use of \"windjamming\" from 1886. The word has evolved to include sail-powered passenger cruise ships."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Herzogin_Cecilie_SLV_AllenGren.jpg/330px-Herzogin_Cecilie_SLV_AllenGren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windjammer","wikidata":"Q573206"},{"title":"Windjammer (1958 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Windjammer is a 1958 documentary film that recorded a 17,500-nautical-mile (32,400 km) voyage of the Norwegian sail training ship Christian Radich. Windjammer was produced by Louis de Rochemont and directed by Louis de Rochemont III. It was the only film to be shot in the widescreen Cinemiracle process, which came with a seven-track stereophonic soundtrack."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d9/Windjammer_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windjammer_(1958_film)","wikidata":"Q446079"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/27/Luther_Little1917.jpg/330px-Luther_Little1917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"h